## Why This Is Asked
Tests dynamic cross-DC routing control and zero-downtime config updates in docker-dca.

## Key Concepts
- etcd as central config store
- sidecar watching and config generation
- nginx config fragmenting and graceful reload
- cross-DC raft replication
- observability via Prometheus

## Code Example

```yaml
# example fragment regenerated by sidecar
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  server_name tenant.example.com;
  location / {
    proxy_pass http://api-primary:8080;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to handle watch failures or conflicts?
- How to scale the sidecar to many tenants?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to implement a policy-driven, per-tenant response shaping mechanism in a docker-dca setup, using a Config object propagated to the service. It demonstrates practical data-safety concerns and integration with Traefik TLS termination.

## Key Concepts

- Docker Config for policy data
- Per-tenant response shaping and JSON filtering
- Payload transformation without altering business logic
- Traefik TLS edge in multi-DC deployments
- Basic end-to-end testing in a docker-dca context

## Code Example

```go
// Go example: filterFields filters payload by allowed keys
func filterFields(in map[string]interface{}, allowed []string) map[string]interface{} {
    out := make(map[string]interface{})
    set := make(map[string]struct{}, len(allowed))
    for _, k := range allowed { set[k] = struct{}{} }
    for k, v := range in {
        if _, ok := set[k]; ok {
            out[k] = v
        }
    }
    return out
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test for a tenant with no allowed fields? What would the response look like?
- What are the security implications if the tenant config is mis-synced between DCs, and how would you detect/mitigate it?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to configure a lightweight canary in a real swarm, using Traefik as a modern edge proxy, and integrate observability with OpenTelemetry. It checks practical networking, TLS setup, and traffic shaping without requiring complex multi-cluster setups.

## Key Concepts

- Docker Swarm overlay networks and service deployment
- Traefik ACME TLS with staging
- Weighted canary routing and health-check-based rollback
- Lightweight OpenTelemetry tracing (export to stdout) and header propagation

